  "verbalization": "Cenobamate is implicated in the interaction with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex through multiple pathways, with DNA polymerase eta serving as a common intermediate in all three evidence streams. The final scores from the three paths suggest that Cenobamate's target is DNA polymerase eta, which is then targeted by different compounds, including Myristyl palmitate and 2-Oxaisodauc-5-En-12-Al. These compounds, in turn, target the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, indicating a potential mechanism by which Cenobamate may influence this complex. The overlapping targets and the presence of multiple compounds that interact with the same complex suggest a possible role for Cenobamate in modulating the activity of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. The evidence supports a relationship between Cenobamate and the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex through a chain of targets, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be elucidated.",
